From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maago <maago@example.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:58:56 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Drafts are their author's

A draft or a scheduled post is not out yet: only its author and staff
see it.

Until now a draft was a status's name and no more. It was on the
board's list and on the post page; 0029 kept back only its files. Now
"not out" means the same everywhere.

- The lists, SQL leaves out: post_list.sql and search_posts.sql get
  p.status <> 'draft' (scheduled posts are out already, with
  publish_at <= :now). export_rows.sql gets :now and both conditions,
  and ExportBoard passes one moment, read once, to every page. On a list
  they show to nobody: their author sees them in /me (0030), staff in
  the admin. Archived posts show
- One post, the views leave out, with one helper:

      func maySee(u *auth.User, p Post) error

  A hidden post, or a draft or scheduled post that u may not change
  (nobody: nil; somebody: mayChange(*u, p)), is sql.ErrNoRows: a 404.
  The pages that read a post answer 404, not 403, so that they do not
  reveal a post that is not out. What changes a post (publish, archive,
  delete, edit, upload) needs a sign-in, and keeps mayChange's 403
- postPage asks maySee, so the post page and the comment ask it in one
  place. Who is asking comes through the signatures:

      func ShowPost(ctx context.Context, u *auth.User, db maago.DB, in ShowPostIn) (PostPage, error)
      func CreateComment(ctx context.Context, u auth.User, tx maago.Tx, in ShowPostIn) (maago.Result[PostPage], error)

  ShowPost is for anybody, so its user is a pointer, nil for nobody;
  CreateComment needs a sign-in, and passes &u. postPage reads the post
  with GetPost for maySee, then PostDetail, whose result has neither the
  author nor publish_at
- DownloadAttachment asks maySee too. A draft's file from somebody else
  was a 403 in 0029, and is a 404 now; a scheduled post's files are
  kept back too. An escape view reads the user from the request, and
  returns no error: it writes http.NotFound itself

New posts still start as drafts. So two things change with it:

- The webhook (0018) hears of a post when it is published, not when it
  is written: right after the write, the link it opens would be a 404.
  The call moves from savePost to moveTo, which publishes, in the same
  maago.AfterCommit. Archiving is no news
- A post written through the API is a draft too, so the frontend needs
  a way to publish: POST /api/posts/{id}/publish returns the published
  post as JSON. move for HTML and APIPublish for the API share moveTo:

      func APIPublish(ctx context.Context, u auth.User, tx maago.Tx, in PostIn) (Post, error)

The tests that read lists make their posts published, or publish them,
first. A new test, TestDrafts, sees what nobody, bob, ann and staff get
from drafts' and scheduled posts' pages, comments and files; that only
published posts show to anybody on the lists, the search, the API and
the CSV; and that the webhook is quiet on writing and archiving, and
hears of publishing, by the time the response is back.

